{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the first.</b> Meaning, if he harvested many fruits at once, he is not obligated to bring every first fruit as firstfruits, but only whichever he wishes of them. And what the Sages, their memory for blessing, said (Bikkurim 1:3) that one may bring only from the seven species — this is learned by a gezerah shavah, for ״אֶרֶץ״ is said here and there (Menachot 84a). And its saying <b>all fruit</b> means all the fruits with which I praised the Land to you." "<b>Which HaShem your Elohim gives you.</b> Meaning, since HaShem reserved for Himself a portion in the Land, namely the sabbatical year (Leviticus 25:4), as it is written ״וּבַשָּׁנָה הַשְּׁבִיעִית שַׁבָּת לַה׳״ — therefore His good word comes to command only for the time of giving to you, which is six years; but the sabbatical year does not involve bringing firstfruits, because they are not his but are ownerless for all."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:01.493994565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}